[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix. Its own cause table says otherwise. Read by
tenant, booking form and body, the reports in #4471 hold three problems. Each one now has its own
ticket.

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

- **`parser`** — the shared parser reads every date month first. A tenant that writes the day
  first gets day and month swapped: 7 April comes out as 4 July. Fixed on 5 October.
- **`hint`** — booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at a day-first
  tenant type what the hint says, and the form reads it the tenant's way. The parser fix does not
  touch it: the form has to print the tenant's order.
- **`one-day`** — the date moves by one day, not by a swap: Tuesday becomes Monday, one client in
  Lisbon and one in Toronto see different days for the same meeting, an invite arrives before the
  booking. That is a time zone problem, not a parser problem. The desk had already marked these
  reports (`desk-notes.json`); its view still counts them under `parser` by tenant, so they are
  counted there too.

## How they were counted

- One id, one report: the export repeats some reports across pages (`uniqueById`).
- Counts are the desk's own view, as exported: the cause comes from the tenant's locale and form
  (`causes.ts`). Never from `intakeTag`: intake guessed from the reporter's browser and disagrees
  with the tenant on dozens of these reports.
- A one-day move comes from what the report says (`desk-notes.json`).
- Every count above is computed from `reports-4471.json` at render time.

<Callout kind="warn">
A matching subject is not the same problem. #4471 holds a dozen different subjects, and five of them
show up under all three problems. Merging on subject alone (decision 0001) is how three
problems ended up as one ticket marked known.
</Callout>

## Outcome

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October:

- **`parser`** — fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Ticket closed as done.
- **`hint`** — won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired. Ticket closed as not planned.
- **`one-day`** — not covered by either. Its ticket stays open until someone finds where an
  invite's date crosses time zones.

New date reports: place them by tenant and body, then merge into the ticket of their problem.

